MongoDB aggregation pipeline processes documents through stages:

db.orders.aggregate([
  { $match: { status: 'completed' } },
  { $group: {
    _id: '$customerId',
    totalAmount: { $sum: '$amount' },
    orderCount: { $sum: 1 },
    avgAmount: { $avg: '$amount' }
  }},
  { $sort: { totalAmount: -1 } },
  { $limit: 10 },
  { $lookup: {
    from: 'customers',
    localField: '_id',
    foreignField: '_id',
    as: 'customer'
  }},
  { $unwind: '$customer' },
  { $project: {
    customerName: '$customer.name',
    totalAmount: 1,
    orderCount: 1
  }}
]);

Common stages: $match (filter), $group (aggregate), $sort, $limit, $skip, $lookup (join), $unwind (flatten arrays), $project (reshape), $addFields.

MongoDB update using aggregation pipeline (MongoDB 4.2+):

// Update with computed values using pipeline
db.products.updateMany(
  { category: 'electronics' },
  [
    { $set: {
      discountPrice: { $multiply: ['$price', 0.9] },
      lastUpdated: '$$NOW',
      fullName: { $concat: ['$brand', ' - ', '$name'] }
    }}
  ]
);

// Conditional update
db.users.updateMany({}, [
  { $set: {
    tier: {
      $switch: {
        branches: [
          { case: { $gte: ['$points', 1000] }, then: 'Gold' },
          { case: { $gte: ['$points', 500] }, then: 'Silver' }
        ],
        default: 'Bronze'
      }
    }
  }}
]);

The pipeline syntax (array of stages) allows using expressions, accessing other fields, and computing values during updates — much more powerful than regular $set.

MongoDB compound index indexes multiple fields together:

// Create compound index
db.orders.createIndex({ customerId: 1, createdAt: -1 });

// This index supports queries on:
db.orders.find({ customerId: '123' }); // Uses index (prefix)
db.orders.find({ customerId: '123', createdAt: { $gt: ISODate('2025-01-01') } }); // Uses full index
db.orders.find({ customerId: '123' }).sort({ createdAt: -1 }); // Uses index for both filter + sort

// Does NOT support:
