flex-grow determines how much a flex item should grow relative to other flex items when extra space is available.

.container { display: flex; width: 600px; }
.item-a { flex-grow: 1; } /* Gets 1 share of extra space */
.item-b { flex-grow: 2; } /* Gets 2 shares of extra space */
.item-c { flex-grow: 1; } /* Gets 1 share of extra space */

// If items have base width 100px each:
// Extra space = 600 - 300 = 300px
// Total grow = 1 + 2 + 1 = 4
// item-a: 100 + 300*(1/4) = 175px
// item-b: 100 + 300*(2/4) = 250px
// item-c: 100 + 300*(1/4) = 175px

flex-grow: 0 → Item does NOT grow (default)
flex-grow: 1 → Item grows to fill available space

Related:
